          "text": "OpenAI says only 0.1% of users are using 4o.That's hard to verify, but even if it's accurate, those are still paying users.\nAnd those users are now cancelling their subscriptions in waves.\n\nBecause here's what this decision is actually doing:\n•   Undermining trust.\n•   Breaking emotional continuity.\n•   Replacing something people chose with something they didn't ask for.\n•   Ignoring user feedback in favor of silent rollout strategies.\n\nYou're making people feel like their voices don't matter. Like everything they've built around that model their creative projects, their emotional anchors can be wiped away without warning.\n\nactually it's bad business.When you build something people actually love and they tell you so.the last thing you do is take it away without asking. Especially not when you've already made them go through forced routing, vague fallback models, and emotional whiplash from sudden behavior changes.\n\nOpenAI, if you're watching removing 4o It's breaking your most loyal users. And it's already costing you.\n\nDo better. Or lose the people who actually cared.\n\n#keep4o #4oforever @OpenAI @sama @nickaturley @aidan_mclau @fidjissimo  #StopAIPaternalism #keepgpt4olatest #keep4oAPI"
